## The Right Shade Is the One That Looks Like You, Only Better

Fair skin is not a limitation. It is a specific canvas with specific rules  and once you know the rules, the decisions stop being frustrating and start being interesting. Undertone first. Finish second. Shade family third. In that order, every time.

The readers who get this right are not the ones with the most confidence about colour. They are the ones who stopped applying medium-skin logic to fair-skin problems. Your vein test result changes everything. Your finish choice changes almost as much. And the right nude, the right red, the right dark shade  chosen with your undertone in mind  will look more like *you* than anything a generic shade list ever suggested.
